cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this project when using or referencing its methods, software, or results."
title: "JOVIAN-AP: Data Assimilation with an OpenFOAM-Based Rotating-Flow Model of Jovian Jets and Vortices"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Koramutla"
    given-names: "Pradeep"
abstract: >
  JOVIAN-AP aims to develop a computational framework for studying
  rotating atmospheric flows inspired by Jupiter's jets and vortices.
  The project investigates the use of numerical fluid dynamics,
  synthetic observations, and data assimilation to improve the
  reconstruction and prediction of atmospheric flow fields. Its
  objectives include implementing and verifying a suitable physical
  model, evaluating data assimilation methods, conducting reproducible
  numerical experiments, and quantitatively assessing forecast accuracy.